Package: roj
Architecture: all
Depends: gjs | nodejs (>= 18), ${misc:Depends}
Description: Kurdish solar calendar on the command line
 roj shows and converts dates in the Kurdish solar calendar, in Sorani,
 Kurmanji, English, Persian or Arabic, with the Gregorian, Persian and
 Islamic calendars beside it. It prints month grids, converts dates,
 formats them with strftime patterns and lists Kurdish events and .ics
 calendars. Roj means both sun and day in Kurdish.

Package: gnome-shell-extension-roj
Architecture: all
Section: gnome
Depends: gnome-shell (>= 45), gjs, ${misc:Depends}
Recommends: roj, gnome-shell-extension-prefs | gnome-shell-extension-manager
Description: Kurdish solar calendar for the GNOME top bar
 Roj puts the Kurdish solar date in the GNOME Shell top bar, in Sorani,
 Kurmanji, English, Persian or Arabic. Every day in its calendar shows
 the Kurdish day with optional Gregorian, Persian and Islamic days, and
 the popup lists Kurdish events and any .ics calendar. It includes a
 date converter, a guide, light and dark themes and settings backup.
